hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"483","Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah and al-Nufayli narrated to us, both saying: Hafs narrated to us, from Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kindness to parents suffices in place of jihad."
"484","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu Hazim, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever strikes his father, kill him. Ibrahim said: I mentioned it to Sufyan, and he said: I have heard it from Abu Hazim."
"485","Ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub, from Ata ibn Dinar al-Hudhali, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, which of the two parents has the greater right? He said: She who carried him between the two sides, suckled him with the two breasts, nursed him upon the two thighs, and ransomed him with both parents."
"486","Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sa'id ibn al-As, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The right of the eldest brother over the younger is the right of the father over his child."
